# reconsider — an act on screen thought over again, and given to a means the click would let through
#
# The wolf in the Test Den is an enemy in the same area, so UnderThreatImpossibleRule refuses any act
# that is not about facing it unless the means is discreet. Woodcraft (pinned) is not: the thinking
# offers "examine the wolf" and the click would refuse it. Reconsider asks a thinking modus mentis to
# keep the act or want no part of it — under --playground it keeps it — and gives it to another means
# able to carry it out on the click as well as before it: a discreet observer — Hunt (granted) or
# Stealth (in the seed-42 kit), whichever the playground draws. The
# old button greys out and no longer answers a click; the new one passes the threat rule. One noetic
# point for the thinking, one for the reconsider.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Den" --period noon --observe-only wolf --grant-mm woodcraft,hunt --organs pineal_gland=0

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
advance 12 180
expect wolf

strategy succeed
goal examine
means woodcraft
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
expect [Woodcraft
regions

# Reconsider the act: any thinking modus mentis, and the means is no longer pinned.
means none
click action 0
choose 2
choose 0
advance 12 180
expect I think again about how to
expect discreetly examine
regions

# The new act passes the threat rule on the click.
click action 1
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect-not while under the threat of
expect SUCCESS
expect-verb examine
quit
